<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb private machinery orders fall 1.6% mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb private machinery orders fall 1.6% mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's private-sector machinery orders, excluding those for machinery at electric power firms and for ships, fell a seasonally adjusted 1.6 percent in February from the previous month to 1.18 trillion yen, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Month-on-month percentage changes, seasonally adjusted, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 FEB	    JAN</p>
<p>Overall	     -6.2	   +16.1</p>
<p> Private	    -1.6	   +11.8</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			 FEB	    JAN</p>
<p> Public	    +13.4	   -11.4</p>
<p> External	  -18.7	   +11.8</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes, not adjusted for seasonal factors, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 FEB	    JAN</p>
<p>Overall	     +1.6	    +9.5</p>
<p> Private	    +9.9	   +14.8</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)  Public	    -25.6	   -35.8</p>
<p> External	   +5.5	   +30.0</p>
</text>
